      </div>
      <div class="blk"><h4>Trader Session Note</h4><p>"Took the London sweep on Gold, got stopped out for 1R, then jumped back in 6 minutes later at double size before the 15m candle closed."</p></div>
      <div class="blk" style="background:#1A2F4A;color:#F4F8FB;padding:16px 18px;border-radius:14px;border-left:4px solid #F5C518;margin:6px 0"><h4 style="color:#F5C518;margin-bottom:6px;font-size:.82rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">改 KAIZEN AI · Behavioral Read</h4><p style="color:#F4F8FB;font-size:.91rem;line-height:1.6">Your bias was not the problem today. Your ego after the first stop was. Trade 1 followed every rule in your playbook and happened to lose. Trade 2 was not a setup, it was you trying to erase how Trade 1 felt. Across your last 14 sessions, your win rate is <b style="color:#F5C518">68% on first entries</b> and drops to <b style="color:#F5C518">18% whenever you enter again within 20 minutes of a loss</b>. Tomorrow's only rule: one stop out means 20 minutes hands off the mouse.</p></div>
